---
import { localeFromPath } from '@portfolio/i18n';
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import LoanCalculator from '../../components/calculators/LoanCalculator';
---
<ToolLayout title="Mortgage calculator" description="Put a possible home into perspective. Explore monthly payments, purchasing power, and the difference your down payment makes." category="Home finance" image="mortgage">
  <LoanCalculator locale={localeFromPath(Astro.url.pathname)} kind="home" client:load />
  <div slot="guide" class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-2"><div class="prose-copy"><h2>Start with a price—or a budget.</h2><p>Monthly payment mode begins with a home price. Purchasing power begins with what you can pay each month. Both use your chosen interest rate, term, and down payment to estimate a fixed-rate mortgage.</p><h2>How does enganche work?</h2><p>Select a down payment from 10% to 95%, in 5% increments. For example, a 20% down payment on a MXN 2,500,000 home is MXN 500,000, leaving MXN 2,000,000 to finance. The minimum here is a simulator setting; actual lender requirements vary.</p></div><div class="prose-copy"><h2>What is included?</h2><p>The estimate includes principal and interest. It excludes property taxes, insurance, appraisal, notary fees, origination fees, closing costs, and homeowners association dues. Add those separately when deciding on a monthly budget.</p><p>The 10.5% annual rate is an illustrative default. Enter your lender’s nominal fixed annual interest rate. CAT or APR can include other costs and should not be substituted for that rate.</p><p>Payment = P × r ÷ (1 − (1 + r)⁻ⁿ), where r is annual interest ÷ 12. At zero interest, the principal is divided equally over the term. A longer term lowers the payment but typically increases total interest.</p></div></div>
</ToolLayout>
